  "DescIdentified": {
    "type": "cexolocstring",
    "value": {
      "0": "The deep mossy wool blurs the silhouette of the one who carries it, turning a person into a mere shadow among the trees. It mutes the sound of a footfall and stills the air around the body, allowing for a passage unseen by the forest's eyes."
    }
  },
  "Description": {
    "type": "cexolocstring",
    "value": {
      "0": "Coarse wool dyed the color of deep moss clings to the frame, woven with fibers that swallow the light. It drapes over the shoulders like a layer of woodland gloom, muffling the rustle of movement against the brush."
    }
  },
